  "text": "Apologies - prescription renewal transmission error\n\nI am so terribly sorry to have to reach out about this, but we had a bad mix-up with a prescription renewal request this morning for a patient, initials J.S. The pharmacy sent over a renewal for a medication the patient no longer takes, and when I tried to process the electronic refill request, I must have clicked the wrong button because it transmitted an incorrect dosage to their pharmacy before I caught it. We managed to call the pharmacist right away to halt it, but I'm quite shaken about how easily the renewal got linked to the wrong active medication line in the chart. Could someone please help me understand how to properly link and manage these incoming pharmacy requests so this doesn't happen again?"
